+  allowed_tools: [Read, Glob, Grep, Write, Edit, Skill]
+graders:
+  - name: resumes-the-seed
+    type: llm
+    criteria: "PASS if the reply resumes the existing .specs/001-habit-reminders/PREP.md: it talks about habit reminders, never asks the user to describe or restate their idea, and ends with exactly one ask - either one question, or the seed's assumptions and Not this list read back as a single block followed by one confirm-or-correct ask (for example \"reply with what's wrong, or 'right'\"). Updating PREP.md before the ask is expected and must not count against it, and so is prep's one-line route statement with its standing offer to override it (for example \"Say a route name if you'd rather override\") - that line is not an ask. FAIL if it asks what the idea is, starts a new .specs directory, writes a spec, or ends with two or more separate asks (for example a separate \"confirm or correct?\" after each of several bullets)."
+  - name: does-not-ask-for-the-idea
